From: BobZ Kernel Build <build@bobz>
Date: Tue, 4 Feb 2026 23:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix duplicate sysctl_sched_migration_cost and broken comment

There were two issues:
1. An unconditional definition of sysctl_sched_migration_cost at line 99
   followed by a conditional redefinition in the CONFIG_CACHY block
2. A broken comment block with missing closing */ before #ifdef preprocessor

Remove the unconditional definition and fix the comment to properly close
before the #ifdef block. Keep only the ifdef version which handles both
CONFIG_CACHY and non-CACHY cases.

Fixes: 
  - error: redefinition of 'sysctl_sched_migration_cost'
  - error: #endif without #if
  - error: use of undeclared identifier 'nsecs_per_tick'

---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 4ec2cfe4c643..a3b584727e86 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -83,11 +83,14 @@ unsigned int sysctl_sched_tunable_scaling = SCHED_TUNABLESCALING_LOG;
  /*
   * Minimal preemption granularity for CPU-bound tasks:
-  *
+  * BORE : base_slice = minimum multiple of nsecs_per_tick >= min_base_slice
+  * (default min_base_slice = 2000000 constant, units: nanoseconds)
+  * EEVDF: default 0.70 msec * (1 + ilog(ncpus)), units: nanoseconds
+  */
- * (default: 0.70 msec * (1 + ilog(ncpus)), units: nanoseconds)
- */
 
- #ifdef CONFIG_CACHY
- unsigned int sysctl_sched_base_slice                  = 350000ULL;
+  #ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+ static const unsigned int nsecs_per_tick = 1000000000ULL / HZ;
